  "term": "tension headache",
  "definition": "A tension headache is a common primary headache that usually feels like a mild to moderate, dull, steady pressure spread across the head, scalp, or neck, often described as a tight band or vise. Its exact cause is unclear, although it has been linked with stress and muscle contraction.",
